From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:38:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sgx_ext: bring dma-buf import back (image extension v8)

TI rolled __DRIimageExtension back from 8 to 7 (a698020), dropping
createImageFromDmaBufs and with it EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import, because
DDK 1.17's buffer import "was never fully functional under Linux". The
implementation was kept (createImageFromFds still reaches it).

wlroots >= 0.14 refuses to create its GLES2 renderer without the
extension and renders every frame into dma-buf EGLImages. On the Nexus Q
(OMAP4460, openpvrsgx 1.17 on Linux 6.18) the import works for that
case: linear XRGB8888 GBM buffers and omapdrm dumb buffers, imported,
bound as an FBO and rendered into, read back correctly through
glReadPixels and through a CPU mmap of the dma-buf over 200 frames
each. Restore version 8 and the entry point.
---
 src/gallium/frontends/sgx/sgx_ext.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/sgx/sgx_ext.c b/src/gallium/frontends/sgx/sgx_ext.c
index 6bf0638..b8d2302 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/sgx/sgx_ext.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/sgx/sgx_ext.c
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@
 /* Maximum version numbers for each supported extension */
 #define PVR_DRI_TEX_BUFFER_VERSION      2
 #define PVR_DRI2_FLUSH_VERSION          4
-#define PVR_DRI_IMAGE_VERSION           7
+#define PVR_DRI_IMAGE_VERSION           8
 #define PVR_DRI2_ROBUSTNESS_VERSION     1
 #define PVR_DRI_PRIORITY_VERSION        1
 #define PVR_DRI2_FENCE_VERSION          1
@@ -1325,6 +1325,7 @@ static __DRIimageExtension pvrDRIImage = {
    .fromPlanar = PVRDRIFromPlanar,
    .createImageFromTexture = PVRDRICreateImageFromTexture,
    .createImageFromFds = PVRDRICreateImageFromFds,
+   .createImageFromDmaBufs = PVRDRICreateImageFromDmaBufs,
 #if defined(EGL_IMG_cl_image)
    .createImageFromBuffer = PVRDRICreateImageFromBuffer,
 #endif
